WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:12.490
32. Frida Kahlo's Paintings and Psychology. The Mexican painter Frida Kahlo, 1907 to 1954,

2
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:19.090
lived a life of extraordinary suffering. She caught a disease called polio when she was only

3
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:26.410
six. She was nearly killed in a bus accident when she was 18. The bus accident left her with

4
00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:32.330
long-lasting injuries that caused her great pain for the rest of her life. Because of these

5
00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:38.050
injuries, she was not able to have children. As a result, she suffered a painful miscarriage

6
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:45.210
when she was 25. The pain in Kahlo's body must have affected her paintings. Though she was an

7
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:52.010
energetic, active, vibrant woman, the pain often made her feel alone. The majority of her paintings

8
00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:59.050
are self-portraits. Kahlo once said, I paint myself because I am so often alone and because

9
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:05.770
I am the subject I know best. She must have felt that her unique pain separated her from other

10
00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:12.530
people. Kahlo often painted her face on the bodies of animals or other people. She painted

11
00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:19.410
her individual suffering, but she also used her face to represent pain in all beings. However,

12
00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:26.570
Kahlo also lived a life of passion and fun. She played sports in school, wore colorful clothes,

13
00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:34.730
danced, studied, and loved. She was very proud of being Mexican and was politically active. These

14
00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:41.850
characteristics are represented in her paintings. She uses bold colors, including lots of reds. She

15
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:49.250
also uses Mexican imagery, such as monkeys and parrots. Frida Kahlo took her pain, combined it

16
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:55.490
with her strong spirit, and turned it into art. Her paintings may make viewers uncomfortable

17
00:01:55.490 --> 00:02:01.250
with their honesty, but Kahlo wasn't the type of person to hold back. If she could suffer and

18
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:05.170
grow, her paintings could make viewers feel and grow as well.
